femto patch for epub-stream 0.1.0
Subject: zip: keep central-directory entries and inflate state off the stack

StreamingZip stores up to 256 CdEntry values in a heapless::Vec inside the
struct and builds its InflateState with Box::new(InflateState::new(..)),
which constructs the state on the stack first.

Store the entries in an alloc Vec with the same 256-entry limit (still
ZipError::CentralDirFull beyond it) and create the inflater with
InflateState::new_boxed. new_boxed needs miniz_oxide's "with-alloc" feature,
so enable it.

femto opens books on a catalog worker with a 64 KiB stack; the inline array
and the temporary inflate state produced stack frames too large for it.

The Cargo.toml hunk is against the normalised manifest in the published
crate. femto's vendored manifest is a hand-written reduction of it; see
vendor/patches/epub-stream/README.md.

--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -111,6 +111,7 @@
 
 [dependencies.miniz_oxide]
 version = "0.9"
+features = ["with-alloc"]
 optional = true
 default-features = false
 
--- a/src/zip.rs
+++ b/src/zip.rs
@@ -1,14 +1,14 @@
